   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Manual Features from Satellite Imagery\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook derives per-LSOA spectral features from a Landsat 8 surface-reflectance scene (2019-08-26, London extent) and uses them as predictors for deprivation. The idea: can spectral band statistics computed over each LSOA polygon capture enough land-use signal to predict IMD scores?\n",
    "\n",
    "### Outline\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Load satellite data (`london_landsat.nc`) — 7 Landsat 8 bands, EPSG:4326, ~36 MB\n",
    "2. Load LSOA boundaries\n",
    "3. Zonal statistics — per-LSOA mean for each band\n",
    "4. Assemble feature table and join to IMD\n",
    "5. Cross-validated model: `IMD ~ Landsat band means`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000002",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data\n",
    "\n",
    "We work with two inputs: a multi-band NetCDF raster derived from Landsat 8 and the London LSOA polygon boundaries (2020 definition) used throughout the workshop."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000003",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas\n",
    "import geopandas\n",
    "import xarray as xr\n",
    "import regionmask"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000004",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Satellite imagery\n",
    "\n",
    "`london_landsat.nc` contains surface reflectance for bands B1–B7 of Landsat 8, reprojected to EPSG:4326. We use the `scipy` engine because the standard `netCDF4` C extension is not available in the WASM kernel."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000005",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sr = xr.open_dataset('london_landsat.nc', engine='scipy')['SR']\n",
    "sr"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000006",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### LSOA boundaries\n",
    "\n",
    "We reuse the geometry column from the embeddings GeoJSON, which already carries the 2020 LSOA definitions for London."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000007",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "lsoa = geopandas.read_file('uk_lsoa_london_embeds_2020.geojson')[['LSOA21CD', 'geometry']].set_index('LSOA21CD')\n",
    "lsoa"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000008",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Zonal statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "We want one row per LSOA with the mean surface reflectance for each of the 7 bands — a 7-feature vector per area.\n",
    "\n",
    "Computing this at full resolution (~30 m pixels, 1504 × 1943 grid) is memory-intensive in the browser. We use two approaches:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Demo (below):** coarsen the raster 8× before masking — fast enough to run live, slightly less precise\n",
    "- **Pre-computed (below):** load `landsat_features.csv`, computed offline at full resolution and bundled with the workshop"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000009",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Demo: coarsened zonal statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "Coarsening by 8× reduces the grid from 1504 × 1943 to ~188 × 243 pixels (~240 m resolution), which is still well within LSOA size (~500 m across) and runs in seconds in the browser."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000010",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sr_coarse = sr.coarsen(x=8, y=8, boundary='trim').mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "mask = regionmask.mask_geopandas(lsoa, sr_coarse.x, sr_coarse.y)\n",
    "\n",
    "band_means = sr_coarse.groupby(mask).mean()\n",
    "band_means['mask'] = lsoa.index.values\n",
    "features_demo = band_means.rename({'mask': 'LSOA21CD'}).to_pandas()\n",
    "features_demo"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000011",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Full-resolution features (pre-computed)\n",
    "\n",
    "`landsat_features.csv` was computed offline at full ~30 m resolution using `regionmask` + numpy `bincount` aggregation. Use this for the modelling section."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000012",
   "metadata": {},
